    <main>
      <section class="tunnel-hero" id="tunnel-x" aria-labelledby="tunnel-x-title">
        <div class="tunnel-shell">
          <div class="tunnel-hero-grid">
            <div class="tunnel-hero-copy reveal">
              <div class="tunnel-product-lockup" aria-label="Tunnel-X">
                <span class="tunnel-product-mark" aria-hidden="true"><img src="assets/tunnel-x/tunnel-x-mark.svg" alt="" width="64" height="64" decoding="async" /></span>
                <span class="tunnel-product-lockup-name">tunnel-x</span>
              </div>
              <p class="tunnel-kicker">Secure-X / product 02 · encrypted data plane</p>
              <h1 id="tunnel-x-title">The secure data plane <span class="tunnel-title-accent">after Auth-X.</span></h1>
              <p class="tunnel-lede">Once Auth-X proves a device, Tunnel-X installs a per-session security association and protects each telemetry frame from ESP32 to sink.</p>
              <div class="tunnel-actions">
                <a class="button-link button-link-primary" href="#tunnel-frame">Inspect the frame <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a>
                <a class="button-link button-link-muted" href="contact.html">Talk through a pilot <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
              </div>
              <p class="tunnel-hero-footnote">Reference path · 16 Apr EDS-3 / ESP32 client → C++ sink</p>
            </div>

            <figure class="tunnel-map reveal" data-delay="120" aria-labelledby="tunnel-map-title">
              <div class="tunnel-map-head">
                <span id="tunnel-map-title">MSG7 / secure data</span>
                <span>Ascon-128 AEAD</span>
              </div>
              <div class="tunnel-map-route" role="img" aria-label="Tunnel-X seals a 21-byte sensor payload with Ascon-128, authenticates the MSG7 header, and sends it to a sink that checks SPI and sequence before decrypting and logging it.">
                <div class="tunnel-map-node">
                  <span>01 / CLIENT</span>
                  <strong>ESP32</strong>
                  <small>serialize / seal</small>
                </div>
                <div class="tunnel-map-channel" aria-hidden="true">
                  <span class="tunnel-map-channel-label">18 B HEADER · ASSOCIATED DATA</span>
                  <span class="tunnel-map-channel-line"></span>
                  <span class="tunnel-map-packet">21 B + 16 B TAG</span>
                </div>
                <div class="tunnel-map-node tunnel-map-node-gateway">
                  <span>02 / SINK</span>
                  <strong>ACCEPT</strong>
                  <small>SPI / SEQ / TAG</small>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="tunnel-map-data">
                <span>NONCE = 8 B SA SALT || 8 B SEQ</span>
                <span>MSG7 / 55 B TOTAL</span>
                <span>JSONL / LOGGED</span>
              </div>
              <figcaption>The sink only decodes after the frame's SPI, sequence, and authentication tag pass.</figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>

          <div class="tunnel-hero-rule">
            <span>Handoff / MSG6 → MSG7</span>
            <span>Auth-X → Tunnel-X</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="tunnel-section tunnel-handoff-section" id="tunnel-handoff" aria-labelledby="tunnel-handoff-title">
        <div class="tunnel-shell">
          <div class="tunnel-section-head reveal">
            <p class="tunnel-section-kicker">Product boundary</p>
            <h2 id="tunnel-handoff-title">The handoff is the product.</h2>
            <p>Auth-X answers “who is connecting?” Tunnel-X answers “what is allowed to cross the session?” The security association is the handoff between them.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="tunnel-handoff-grid">
            <article class="tunnel-handoff-stage reveal">
              <span class="tunnel-handoff-index">01</span>
              <div>
                <h3>Auth-X</h3>
                <p>PSK/HMAC admission, challenge proof, X25519 exchange, and session-key derivation.</p>
              </div>
              <span class="tunnel-handoff-state">through MSG6</span>
            </article>
            <div class="tunnel-handoff-connector" aria-hidden="true">
              <span>SA active</span>
              <strong>→</strong>
            </div>
            <article class="tunnel-handoff-stage tunnel-handoff-stage-current reveal" data-delay="100">
              <span class="tunnel-handoff-index">02</span>
              <div>
                <h3>Tunnel-X</h3>
                <p>Ascon-128 frames, SPI/sequence enforcement, gateway decode, and policy-led rekey.</p>
              </div>
              <span class="tunnel-handoff-state">MSG7 onward</span>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="tunnel-section tunnel-frame-section" id="tunnel-frame" aria-labelledby="tunnel-frame-title">
        <div class="tunnel-shell">
          <div class="tunnel-section-head reveal">
            <p class="tunnel-section-kicker">Inside MSG7 / secure data</p>
            <h2 id="tunnel-frame-title">Every frame carries its own decision context.</h2>
            <p>Tunnel-X gives the gateway enough structure to reject a bad frame before the application sees it.</p>
          </div>

          <dl class="tunnel-frame-ledger">
            <div class="tunnel-frame-row reveal">
              <dt>Associated data</dt>
              <dd>18-byte header with version, algorithm, SPI, sequence, and payload length, authenticated with the frame.</dd>
              <span>HEADER</span>
            </div>
            <div class="tunnel-frame-row reveal" data-delay="60">
              <dt>Protected payload</dt>
              <dd>21-byte sensor record sealed with Ascon-128 AEAD and carried with a 16-byte authentication tag.</dd>
              <span>PAYLOAD</span>
            </div>
            <div class="tunnel-frame-row reveal" data-delay="120">
              <dt>Nonce discipline</dt>
              <dd>Every frame derives a 16-byte nonce from the SA’s 8-byte salt and its 8-byte sequence number.</dd>
              <span>NONCE</span>
            </div>
            <div class="tunnel-frame-row reveal" data-delay="180">
              <dt>Gateway decision</dt>
              <dd>The sink checks SPI and the next sequence, verifies the tag, decodes the sample, and appends per-peer JSONL telemetry.</dd>
              <span>ACCEPT</span>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="tunnel-section tunnel-rekey-section" id="tunnel-rekey" aria-labelledby="tunnel-rekey-title">
        <div class="tunnel-shell">
          <div class="tunnel-section-head reveal">
            <p class="tunnel-section-kicker">Security-association lifecycle</p>
            <h2 id="tunnel-rekey-title">Rotate the session without dropping TCP.</h2>
            <p>Rekeying is an in-band state transition, not a reconnect. The policy can use the default 24-hour age, a custom time, or a packet-count threshold.</p>
          </div>

          <ol class="tunnel-rekey-ledger">
            <li class="tunnel-rekey-row reveal">
              <span class="tunnel-rekey-code">MSG12</span>
              <h3>Set the policy</h3>
              <p>The sink sends the active SA’s rekey policy under the current session key.</p>
              <span class="tunnel-rekey-state">policy</span>
            </li>
            <li class="tunnel-rekey-row reveal" data-delay="80">
              <span class="tunnel-rekey-code">MSG8 → MSG9</span>
              <h3>Negotiate fresh material</h3>
              <p>Both sides contribute fresh X25519 key material, nonces, a new salt, and a new SPI.</p>
              <span class="tunnel-rekey-state">pending SA</span>
            </li>
            <li class="tunnel-rekey-row reveal" data-delay="160">
              <span class="tunnel-rekey-code">MSG10 → MSG11</span>
              <h3>Confirm, then switch</h3>
              <p>The new SA is confirmed with its derived key; the old association is superseded on the same TCP session.</p>
              <span class="tunnel-rekey-state">active SA</span>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="tunnel-section tunnel-reference-section" id="tunnel-reference" aria-labelledby="tunnel-reference-title">
        <div class="tunnel-shell">
          <div class="tunnel-reference-grid">
            <div class="tunnel-reference-copy reveal">
              <p class="tunnel-section-kicker">Reference build</p>
              <h2 id="tunnel-reference-title">Small frames. Explicit state. Useful logs.</h2>
              <p>These are implementation facts from the 16 Apr EDS-3 pipeline. They are not universal performance promises.</p>
            </div>
            <dl class="tunnel-reference-list reveal" data-delay="120">
              <div>
                <dt>05</dt>
                <dd>concurrent client sessions accepted by the sink</dd>
              </div>
              <div>
                <dt>25</dt>
                <dd>received frames between persisted sequence checkpoints</dd>
              </div>
              <div>
                <dt>24<span>h</span></dt>
                <dd>default security-association age policy</dd>
              </div>
              <div>
                <dt>JSONL</dt>
                <dd>per-peer raw telemetry records at the gateway</dd>
              </div>
            </dl>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="tunnel-section tunnel-cta-section" id="tunnel-pilot" aria-labelledby="tunnel-pilot-title">
        <div class="tunnel-shell">
          <div class="tunnel-cta reveal">
            <div>
              <h2 id="tunnel-pilot-title">Own the boundary after identity.</h2>
              <p>Bring an ESP32-class device path or gateway protocol. We’ll map the payload, SA lifecycle, and operating policy.</p>
            </div>
            <a class="button-link button-link-primary" href="contact.html">Talk through a pilot <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

